00:02:47.020 --> 00:02:47.700
is Mad.

61
00:02:47.920 --> 00:02:49.520
Pam is pissed off.

62
00:02:50.000 --> 00:02:56.460
We had a fan question from Kiana and Andres from Williams, Oregon, who said,

63
00:02:56.460 --> 00:02:59.460
We love ourselves an angry Pam.

64
00:02:59.840 --> 00:03:04.100
Our question is, what did you do to get yourself into this mode of angry?

65
00:03:04.380 --> 00:03:07.780
Was it difficult since Pam is usually pretty calm?

66
00:03:08.720 --> 00:03:09.820
Oh, Angela.

67
00:03:12.520 --> 00:03:14.900
This was so difficult for me.

68
00:03:15.800 --> 00:03:19.620
As an actor, this episode, I really, really struggled.

69
00:03:20.200 --> 00:03:22.360
Well, I thought you crushed it, Jenna.

70
00:03:22.580 --> 00:03:23.180
I loved it.

71
00:03:23.260 --> 00:03:25.280
I laughed so much watching it.

72
00:03:25.400 --> 00:03:29.500
And for once, it was nice that someone was more angry than my character.

73
00:03:30.100 --> 00:03:31.940
I guess I can see that.

74
00:03:32.600 --> 00:03:40.400
Well, for me, Angela, I just really struggled with how confrontational Pam was in this episode

75
00:03:40.400 --> 00:03:47.060
because I never felt her as a confrontational person.

76
00:03:47.300 --> 00:03:48.560
So, does Pam get mad?

77
00:03:48.780 --> 00:03:49.200
Oh, sure.

78
00:03:49.200 --> 00:03:49.820
She does.

79
00:03:50.120 --> 00:03:54.400
But she's a, like, silent sufferer.

80
00:03:54.660 --> 00:03:56.080
Does that make sense?

81
00:03:56.340 --> 00:03:56.660
Like...

82
00:03:56.660 --> 00:03:56.980
Oh, yeah.

83
00:03:57.120 --> 00:03:57.920
It does make sense.

84
00:03:58.060 --> 00:04:03.320
But in this one, she is almost like a hostile teenager.

85
00:04:03.860 --> 00:04:10.580
I had a lot of conversations with the creative team about this because I just could not make

86
00:04:10.580 --> 00:04:15.140
that leap from the Pam I had been playing to the Pam that was scripted in this episode.

87
00:04:15.740 --> 00:04:22.320
And, you know, what we decided was that everyone has a breaking point that makes them behave

88
00:04:22.320 --> 00:04:24.160
out of character for themselves.

89
00:04:24.460 --> 00:04:25.760
And this was it.

90
00:04:25.760 --> 00:04:30.960
Michael dating Pam's mom was the thing that was going to show us a whole new side of Pam.

91
00:04:31.280 --> 00:04:32.680
I agree with that.

92
00:04:32.940 --> 00:04:39.600
I mean, you know, we all have someone that is in our lives.

93
00:04:39.600 --> 00:04:44.200
And if they became part of our family, we'd be like, uh-uh-uh, no, no, no, no, no.

94
00:04:44.960 --> 00:04:46.680
So, I believed it.

95
00:04:47.120 --> 00:04:47.320
Yeah.

96
00:04:47.780 --> 00:04:52.640
Strangely, even watching this episode, I was like, did I do it?

97
00:04:53.280 --> 00:04:56.900
Was it, like, it just doesn't seem like Pam to me?

98
00:04:57.080 --> 00:04:58.400
It's so crazy.

99
00:04:58.980 --> 00:05:03.260
Jenna, not only did you do it, but as your BFF, I have to brag on you a little bit.

100
00:05:03.340 --> 00:05:07.540
I found an article in researching this episode that I wanted to read to you.

101
00:05:08.180 --> 00:05:08.660
Okay.

102
00:05:09.280 --> 00:05:14.880
It was written by Nathan Rabin for the AV Club, and it's still on their website.

103
00:05:15.180 --> 00:05:16.580
I'm just going to share a little bit of it.

104
00:05:17.220 --> 00:05:22.580
Nathan writes, many years ago, back when I worked at a thrift store, a singularly unpleasant

105
00:05:22.580 --> 00:05:28.320
coworker I'd had a bitter falling out with ambled up to me and awkwardly asked for the

106
00:05:28.320 --> 00:05:30.140
phone number of one of my sisters.

107
00:05:30.140 --> 00:05:33.320
I will never forget my reaction.

108
00:05:33.680 --> 00:05:42.200
Without thought, without premeditation, I shouted, no, and stormed away in a huff.

109
00:05:42.400 --> 00:05:44.880
I did not merely refuse his requeSt.

110
00:05:45.180 --> 00:05:51.360
I responded with revulsion, visceral horror, and something resembling rage.

111
00:05:51.600 --> 00:05:57.120
I am not proud of how I reacted, but if I had to do it over again, I would respond the

112
00:05:57.120 --> 00:05:57.680
same way.

113
00:05:57.680 --> 00:06:00.720
It really was the only sane reaction.

114
00:06:01.200 --> 00:06:06.680
There's something deeply unnerving about our friends, our coworkers, having sex with our

115
00:06:06.680 --> 00:06:11.860
relatives that grows infinitely creepier the less sure we are about the friends or coworkers

116
00:06:11.860 --> 00:06:12.700
in question.

117
00:06:13.060 --> 00:06:16.580
I'm not just saying this because I am deeply, deeply repressed.

118
00:06:16.760 --> 00:06:23.520
So I knew exactly how Jim and Pam felt when they found out that Michael had, in his deliciously,

119
00:06:23.800 --> 00:06:27.300
pointlessly formal turn of phrase, taken a lover.

120
00:06:27.680 --> 00:06:30.580
And the lover in question was Pam's mom.

121
00:06:30.820 --> 00:06:34.400
The writing and the acting really sold the can't-miss premise.

122
00:06:34.780 --> 00:06:37.740
It was a half hour of awkward awesomeness.

123
00:06:37.860 --> 00:06:42.460
And I'm not even mentioning the niftiness of Ryan's fedora of mystery.

124
00:06:42.460 --> 00:06:44.800
Oh, my gosh.

125
00:06:44.920 --> 00:06:46.640
I love that article.

126
00:06:47.040 --> 00:06:47.960
Isn't that so great?

127
00:06:47.960 --> 00:06:50.700
I thought you would feel affirmed in your performance.

128
00:06:51.180 --> 00:06:51.800
I do.

129
00:06:51.980 --> 00:06:57.440
And basically what he is saying is what Gene and Lee kept saying to me every day.

130
00:06:57.720 --> 00:07:00.880
They were like, you cannot help this.

131
00:07:01.280 --> 00:07:04.540
This is coming out of you and you can't stop it.

132
00:07:04.700 --> 00:07:06.020
That was their direction.

133
00:07:06.020 --> 00:07:07.980
I agree with Nathan.

134
00:07:08.240 --> 00:07:08.620
Amazing.

135
00:07:08.900 --> 00:07:12.360
Also, his response to his coworker was so hilarious.

136
00:07:13.800 --> 00:07:14.480
All right.

137
00:07:14.720 --> 00:07:17.280
Moving us to fast fact number two.

138
00:07:17.880 --> 00:07:23.440
This one is all about our B story, which I'm calling Dwight Records Jim.

139
00:07:23.960 --> 00:07:25.140
I got curious.

140
00:07:25.560 --> 00:07:26.600
Oh, I did too.

141
00:07:26.600 --> 00:07:29.100
