142
00:07:29.700 --> 00:07:31.980
Here was what I wanted to know.

143
00:07:32.620 --> 00:07:35.720
I was like, Dwight is committing a crime, right?

144
00:07:36.620 --> 00:07:36.920
Yeah.

145
00:07:37.500 --> 00:07:38.700
This is a crime.

146
00:07:39.060 --> 00:07:39.840
Pretty sure.

147
00:07:40.380 --> 00:07:41.600
I looked it up.

148
00:07:41.820 --> 00:07:43.280
Would mom detectives know?

149
00:07:44.200 --> 00:07:48.000
By the way, this whole storyline, I made a note to myself.

150
00:07:48.240 --> 00:07:50.380
Remember this for mom detectives.

151
00:07:53.000 --> 00:08:03.560
In 38 states, you can record a private conversation with another person and you only need one

152
00:08:03.560 --> 00:08:06.560
person to know that there's a recording happening.

153
00:08:06.700 --> 00:08:08.920
It's called one party consent.

154
00:08:09.300 --> 00:08:11.180
So would the party then be Dwight?

155
00:08:11.360 --> 00:08:12.880
Is Dwight the consent party?

156
00:08:13.140 --> 00:08:13.600
Yes.

157
00:08:13.880 --> 00:08:14.220
Oh.

158
00:08:14.620 --> 00:08:16.080
So he is recording.

159
00:08:16.500 --> 00:08:17.980
Well, I guess he's not in there.

160
00:08:18.380 --> 00:08:19.120
Exactly.

161
00:08:20.380 --> 00:08:23.800
So basically, he would need someone like Creed in cahoots with him.

162
00:08:24.060 --> 00:08:30.200
Basically, everyone who is talking to Jim would need to know they're being recorded.

163
00:08:32.200 --> 00:08:40.160
But there are 12 states that have a two-party consent law, and that means that everybody being

164
00:08:40.160 --> 00:08:43.740
recorded has to give their consent to being recorded.

165
00:08:44.000 --> 00:08:44.300
Right.

166
00:08:44.300 --> 00:08:52.560
And those states are California, Delaware, Florida, Illinois, Maryland, Massachusetts,

167
00:08:53.500 --> 00:08:59.660
Montana, Nevada, New Hampshire, Washington, and Pennsylvania.

168
00:09:00.500 --> 00:09:01.000
Hmm.

169
00:09:01.000 --> 00:09:03.860
So he is breaking the law.

170
00:09:04.060 --> 00:09:05.280
He is breaking the law.

171
00:09:05.400 --> 00:09:06.380
Now, there are exceptions.

172
00:09:07.120 --> 00:09:12.560
You can videotape or record anything in a public space, but this is not a public space.

173
00:09:12.960 --> 00:09:19.740
Or you can record a private conversation in a private space if you reasonably suspect that

174
00:09:19.740 --> 00:09:26.200
the person you're recording is about to commit or is in the process of committing a violent

175
00:09:26.200 --> 00:09:26.760
crime.

176
00:09:26.760 --> 00:09:27.300
Oh.

177
00:09:28.040 --> 00:09:29.300
None of these things apply.

178
00:09:29.700 --> 00:09:31.360
What Dwight is doing is totally illegal.

179
00:09:31.560 --> 00:09:35.960
In fact, in Pennsylvania, it is a felony in the third degree.

180
00:09:36.440 --> 00:09:41.180
And if he was convicted, he could face three and a half years to seven years in prison and

181
00:09:41.180 --> 00:09:42.700
a fine of up to $15,000.

182
00:09:43.260 --> 00:09:44.920
And you know who would have known that?

183
00:09:45.400 --> 00:09:45.880
Dwight.

184
00:09:46.180 --> 00:09:46.660
Dwight.

185
00:09:47.200 --> 00:09:48.640
He's knowingly breaking the law.

186
00:09:48.820 --> 00:09:49.400
He is.

187
00:09:49.880 --> 00:09:51.420
And what does he get out of it?

188
00:09:52.060 --> 00:09:52.640
Nothing.

189
00:09:53.580 --> 00:09:55.540
Eight hours of paper talk.

190
00:09:56.100 --> 00:09:58.220
Eight hours of, yeah, sales calls.

191
00:09:58.420 --> 00:09:59.100
Paper talk.

192
00:09:59.780 --> 00:10:00.700
All right, Angela.

